From lgautier at gmail.com  Tue Feb  5 10:48:45 2013
From: lgautier at gmail.com (Laurent Gautier)
Date: Tue, 05 Feb 2013 18:48:45 +0800
Subject: [Rpy] Embracing Python 3 - rpy2-2.4.0-dev
Message-ID: <5110E38D.2090709@gmail.com>

Hi,

The default branch for rpy2 (currently 2.4.0-dev is no longer supporting 
Python 2).

I believe that this is not such a radical move, since an increasing 
number of Linux distributions have Python 3 as a default, and this will 
simplify the code base (particularly at the C level).

While Python 3 will be the way forward for new features and additions, 
the 2.3.x series for rpy2 will remain compatible with both Python 2.7 
and Python 3.3 and have bugfix releases along the way, until rpy2-2.4.0 
is out.



Laurent

